/ayra
*.test

# The catalogue is a program, and building it in place leaves the binary beside
# its source under the same name as its directory.
/catalogue/catalogue

# The approved pictures are kept; what a failed comparison writes beside them is
# not. A picture named for the run that produced it is a diagnostic, and a
# diagnostic committed once is a diagnostic committed for ever.
*.failed.png

# Where the published tree and the README examples are staged to be compiled.
# Both are made and removed by the test that uses them; a crash leaves one
# behind and nothing that lands here belongs in the history.
.published-compile-check/
.published-flow-check/
.readme-compile-check/

# Harness configuration. It lives at the root of the working tree, not here: one
# file per repository has already diverged, and the commit-msg hook in
# .githooks/ is the layer that actually refuses AI attribution.
.claude/
